Description: Preserve Darwin system directory symlinks during removal
 Darwin's /etc, /tmp and /var are symlinks to /private/etc, /private/tmp
 and /private/var. A package with files under /etc lists "/etc" as one of
 its directories, and removing it as a symlink to a directory would cut
 the system off from /private/etc. dpkg keeps those. It also keeps any
 other symlink to a directory that still has entries, as it keeps a
 non-empty directory.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04

